WEBVTT

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.440
<i>[Uhtred] I was born</i>
<i>an Aelderman of England.</i>

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.360
<i>True heir to the Northumbrian lands</i>
<i>of Bebbanburg.</i>

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.520
<i>I was 12 years old</i>
<i>when I first went to war.</i>

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.440
<i>I saw my father killed.</i>

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:21.440
<i>Stolen by the invaders,</i>
<i>along with a Saxon girl, Brida,</i>

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:25.520
<i>I became first a slave</i>
<i>and then a son to Earl Ragnar.</i>

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.920
<i>Fate had made me a Dane.</i>

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.800
<i>Had made Young Ragnar my brother</i>

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.640
<i>and Brida, my lover.</i>

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.240
<i>And then fate brought betrayal.</i>

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.840
Fire!

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.960
<i>Lies were thrown to the wind</i>
<i>saying I had killed Ragnar.</i>

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.280
<i>So, taking his hidden wealth,</i>
<i>we fled south...</i>

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.200
<i>...to Wessex.</i>

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.600
<i>To Beocca...</i>

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.040
<i>and to the king's brother, Alfred.</i>

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.280
<i>Seen by the Danes as a Saxon,</i>
<i>and by the Saxons as a Dane,</i>

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:01.200
<i>my word could not be trusted.</i>

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.920
<i>But I am Uhtred, son of Uhtred,</i>
<i>and destiny is all.</i>

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.720
Stand clear, it is the king!

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.240
I have to speak, Lord.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:52.800
The axe cut deep.
Even a king couldn't survive that wound.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.480
We shall pray and we shall see.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:26.920
Apologies, Lord, this is the best I could
do without first speaking to Alfred.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:31.720
I have brought food and ale
and more importantly, good news.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:32.960
Alfred is dead?

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.000
The opposite.
He is alive and he is victorious.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:38.920
We defeated the Danes.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.680
[yelling]

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:42.960
Why is this good news?

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:44.600
Alfred acted upon your advice.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:45.800
You share in his glory.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:50.760
Glory?! Then why is he caged
and left to shit in the corner?

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.440
You call that glory?

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.600
Can she not hold her tongue
for just one moment?

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:57.840
No, she can not and she will not!

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.480
Keep your food, I don't want it!

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.880
I will not eat or drink
until I am set free!

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:03.480
Only Alfred can order your release!

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:04.760
I will speak with him!

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:08.480
You should spend this time, girl,
to contemplate your improvement.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.640
I will use this time to curse you.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:13.760
Then do it!

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.760
Alfred refused my sword.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.640
I won't be offering it again
unless he begs.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:23.080
Lord, sometimes I wonder
whether your pig-headedness

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.520
is not simple stupidity.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:28.120
He will send for you when he has scraped
the mud and blood from his mail.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.480
We will give thanks to Odin
for our deliverance.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:32.880
Do that!

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:35.160
We are Danes!

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:37.560
[guard] Show respect!

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:42.080
Do it again and I will cut you
prick to throat.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.960
You're a hero of Wessex.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:03:59.840
Congratulations.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.240
We're alive.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:07.520
[Alfred] What is it?

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:12.200
I couldn't wait to see you.

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:15.520
I was told you are safe,
but I needed proof.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.240
Here it is.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:22.800
Leave us. My wife will help me.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:24.320
My Lord.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:28.480
My privilege.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:36.040
Ensure it is repaired and well.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:38.920
I'd be a lost fool without you.

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:44.800
[sighs]

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.360
Fingers and thumbs.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:54.600
[knocking]

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:57.120
Who knocks!?

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:58.520
My Lord.

00:04:58.600 --> 00:04:59.600
My Lady.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.800
Forgive me, I was hoping for a moment

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.920
to discuss the Aelderman Uhtred.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.760
Father, forgive me,
but my Lord is in need of rest.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:13.120
He is. You are...

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:14.880
Forgive me.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:34.040
Aethelwold. Were you on the hill?
I didn't see you.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:38.880
I was kept safe with the priests.

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:46.960
There will be other battles, many.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:50.160
And on and on it will go, I'm sure,
until we are all dead.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.880
You saying we should surrender?

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:55.480
Never... never.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:59.080
But I am not against compromise.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:03.040
As much as I love my God,
I am in no hurry to reach Heaven.

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:06.000
I fear no number
of kneeling clergy men will change

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:08.200
what a heathen's axe has already decreed.

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:10.400
Our prayers should be
with the king's successor,

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:11.480
whoever that may be.

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:17.200
The crown is mine, my birthright.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.200
You disagree?

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:22.560
The argument against
will be that you are young, Lord.

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:24.360
I am my father's heir!

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:25.800
Yes, you are your father's heir,

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:27.800
but your father was also bonded to Alfred.

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:32.160
A son comes before a brother.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:39.480
Then perhaps you should speak
to the king directly.

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:45.000
Tis my thinking, Lord,
that if on his death bed,

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:47.360
your father were to name you
as his successor,

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:51.000
the Witan would find it difficult
to go against him.

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:54.400
I believe your father would only be
too happy to whisper in your ear,

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.680
whether he was conscious or not.

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:04.560
Your counsel will not be forgotten,
Young Odda.

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:07.200
Thank you, Lord.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:21.400
Guthrum, you went into battle without me.

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:22.760
Why was that?

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:24.480
That was not the intention.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.600
Is that so?

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:30.760
Then why did it happen?

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.120
Let's talk inside.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:34.840
We will talk here.

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:38.080
They marched sooner than we expected,

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:40.680
and they positioned themselves
well on the hill.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.160
It will not happen again.

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:43.600
No. It will not happen again

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:45.920
because you have lost half your men.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.440
We killed their king, Aethelred.

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:51.360
Did you see him fall?

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:53.160
Yeah, I saw him fall.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:56.680
He took an axe. He's dead.
We were not beaten.

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:59.960
Hmm... you want to become King of Wessex.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.160
I will allow that.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:02.280
But where is my payment?

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:03.520
My silver, my grain?

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:05.240
It was promised, but now it has gone.

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:06.320
It's still there.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:08.520
Danes do not lose.

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:09.640
I have not lost.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:13.120
You have given them hope,
Guthrum, that is worse.

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:16.280
Without the king, there is no hope.

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:26.360
If they've defeated the Danes,
which I won't believe,

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:28.040
why aren't they feasting?

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:32.040
The priest doesn't lie,
despite him being a priest.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.400
Why are they so different?

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:38.560
So miserable.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:40.320
God's wish.

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:44.760
I won't become a Saxon woman.

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:47.000
I won't wash, work the fields,
till I drop and cook.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:48.200
It won't come to that.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:49.160
That won't be my life.

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:50.520
Alfred can help us.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:52.800
We'll use him...

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:56.920
...for shelter and then for wealth.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:00.960
He has used you.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.200
And now he owes me.

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:09.600
[bell tolls]

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:12.560
[pig snorts]

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:14.280
[gasps]

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:28.080
Good morning.

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:36.000
My thanks for last night.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.040
[rooster crows]

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:53.560
Open the door, I wish to see my father.

00:09:55.880 --> 00:10:00.200
Open the door,
or I'll have your balls for sling-shot.

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:03.320
Aethelwold.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:06.160
I am here to pray for my father,
the king; to be at his side.

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:07.880
The king is dead.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:11.280
Why was I not called?

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:12.680
I should have been at his side.

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:13.800
You could not be found.

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:15.600
I was sleeping in my chamber.

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:49.560
Before he passed, the king
named me as heir to the throne.

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:55.280
That's what he told me.

00:10:55.360 --> 00:11:00.400
It's the truth... his last wish.

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:02.720
His last command.

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:06.960
You would all do well to repeat this.

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:15.280
I'll inform the Witan of your claim.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:16.640
You should.

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:19.040
Although each person here, and more,

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:22.880
heard your father
bequeath his crown to Alfred.

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:25.840
He must have been delirious.

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:28.240
On which occasion?

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:33.840
I am the son of the king.

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:37.000
Do your duty.

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:49.480
My Lord.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.400
Ah, Uhtred.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:54.080
Please accept my apology
for the delay in your release.

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:56.240
I had other matters to attend.

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:58.360
Ale, Father?

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:01.400
A little, and for our guests.

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:03.000
It seems you spoke the truth.

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:04.440
I did.

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:07.320
Though I realize our victory is temporary,

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:09.080
I am indebted.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:10.600
Wessex is indebted.

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:12.520
Is my apology enough?

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:14.480
It's not, Lord.

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:17.040
What Uhtred means
is that it is not necessary.

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:20.040
I wish to be seen as an Aelderman.
Because I am an Aelderman.

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:21.480
In Northumbria. This is Wessex.

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:22.680
This is England.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:24.800
One kingdom is what you said.

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:26.560
You are without lands, completely.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.080
Then that's what I want.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:29.400
That's what I deserve, land.

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:35.240
I brought you here
solely to convey my thanks,

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:37.320
but we shall talk further at some point.

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:39.560
Now I have other more important
matters to attend.

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:42.200
I gave you victory, Lord,
what's more important than that?

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:43.280
The king is dead.

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:46.640
Since when?

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:48.400
I have not long left him.

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:54.120
My first act as king
will be to offer the Danes a peace.

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:58.880
They will think you spineless... Lord.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:01.480
Then I must convince them otherwise.

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:04.880
Girl, bring some fruit to my chamber.

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:06.680
Some chopped apples and milk.

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:08.600
Rest, wash, eat well.

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:09.840
You have earned it.

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:15.400
What are you saying?

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:17.760
You do not speak to a future king
in that manner.

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:19.840
He is not my Lord and he won't be my king.

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:21.520
Hear me clearly, Uhtred.

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:23.280
Alfred is the man to follow.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:25.920
He is your way back to Bebbanburg,
as Lord and master.

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:30.560
Uhtred's path is Uhtred's business,
not that of a priest.

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:33.040
Forgive me, Lord!

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:36.600
I must leave, pray for strength

00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:39.440
to expunge these unholy thoughts
that fill my mind.

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:48.680
You want land in Wessex?

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:50.760
It's my way back to Bebbanburg.

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:55.520
Any silver you find under Alfred
will be taken by the Danes,

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:57.400
along with your life.

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:58.480
They can't be beaten.

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:01.920
Why are you doing this?

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:03.320
I've said, wealth.

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:18.200
Excuse me, my Lord,
I am on an errand to my Lord Alfred.

00:14:18.280 --> 00:14:19.800
The milk is for Alfred?

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:21.400
It is.

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:29.560
Not a word.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:32.280
Go on.

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:42.840
[breathing heavily]

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:47.560
Master Aethelwold.

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:50.800
The man-child who would have
himself be king.

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:52.840
Out of respect for the late king,

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:56.960
Alfred wishes no to harm to be done
to a hair on your ugly head,

00:14:57.040 --> 00:15:00.440
but he will not put up
with your insolence and lies.

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:03.280
Your own son is party
to my so-called insolence.

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:04.360
Quiet!

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:08.400
Don't you involve others
in your conspiracies.

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:12.800
My head is not ugly.

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:18.240
You're to be sent to Hampton,
to a monastery, to be educated.

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:20.360
It will be a very long process.

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:22.000
I am the king's son!

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:24.120
Wessex cannot afford division.

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:27.320
Nor can it afford the ramblings
of an idiot child,

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:28.960
noble or otherwise.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.440
See to it.

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:34.080
May I make him docile, Lord?

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:35.720
I wish you would.

00:15:35.800 --> 00:15:37.800
[Aethelwold] No, no, no, no!

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:41.040
[knocking]

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:42.680
[Alfred] Come!

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:46.920
Lord, you wished to see me.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:49.760
I did, I did.

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:55.200
You will take a message
to Guthrum, to the Danes.

00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:58.080
You will invite them to negotiate
within days

00:15:58.160 --> 00:15:59.520
but at their own convenience.

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:02.560
If it is a messenger you require, Lord,

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:04.880
there are plenty
within the palace grounds.

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:07.760
It is not a messenger I require,
it is a representative.

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:10.560
You will speak for me.

00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:12.720
Odda, you will speak as me.

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:17.000
Nothing can be written for the Danes.

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:20.440
My letters would be meaningless,
therefore the words spoken

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:22.520
must be my words,

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:26.120
and I entrust them to you.

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:30.120
Then I shall gladly be
your representative, Lord.

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:32.320
Thank you.

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:40.520
Do I offend you?

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:42.000
Watching you.

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:45.000
No, my Lord... never.

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:49.240
I will defend you with my life.

00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:54.840
You stand as everything that is
precious, you are Wessex, England.

00:16:54.920 --> 00:16:58.120
Always to be cherished,
never to be violated.

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:02.720
Only to be loved... vigorously.

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:03.800
[knocking]

00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:04.880
Who is it?

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:06.320
-[door opens]
-My Lord.

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:08.160
My conscience.

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:12.880
My Lord, would you care
to join me in prayer, perhaps,

00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:14.520
for the passing of the king?

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:17.280
I will, Father. I give you my thanks.

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:21.440
Forgive me, my Lord, the milk has soured.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.840
I am tired of milk and apples.

00:17:29.920 --> 00:17:31.160
I need meat.

00:17:31.240 --> 00:17:33.520
But you are a martyr, my Lord, to meat.

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:35.480
My Lord needs feeding!

00:17:35.560 --> 00:17:38.200
My Lord is not a saint and never shall be!

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:40.640
I have survived battle, I need meat!

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:46.400
We shall pray together, my Lord,
for strength.

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:48.960
Why does it have to be a sin?

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:59.720
Already, it is a burden.

00:18:01.840 --> 00:18:04.800
It seems never to be about
what I would wish to do.

00:18:04.880 --> 00:18:07.600
It is about what I must do.

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:13.600
Ask God to give me the strength

00:18:13.680 --> 00:18:15.960
to wear the crown as well as you.

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:28.320
Father Beocca. A moment.

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:29.640
Yes, Lord.

00:18:29.720 --> 00:18:32.280
Uhtred may well have a use.

00:18:32.360 --> 00:18:35.160
I'm pleased that is what you think, Lord.

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:37.040
This Brida, she is what to him?

00:18:37.120 --> 00:18:38.440
I would say a hindrance, Lord.

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:39.520
A wife?

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:40.960
No, no, never. No, no.

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:42.560
She is restless.

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:44.440
She is the devil on his shoulder, I fear.

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:46.120
But he is fond of her.

00:18:47.320 --> 00:18:49.840
Yes, that is his way.

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:51.720
We shall see.

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:53.120
Thank you.

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:54.200
My Lord.

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:27.120
I carry a message.

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:29.480
From King Alfred.

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:31.080
Who is King Alfred?

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:33.200
He is Alfred, King of Wessex.

00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:36.000
He invites the Earl Guthrum
to negotiate a peace.

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:37.960
You are Guthrum?

00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:40.200
Get down from your horse, boy.

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:44.400
Get down from your horse and look at me.

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:52.520
You are a beauty.

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:57.720
Tell this king, what was his name?

00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:59.760
Alfred.

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:03.960
Tell King Alfred that
Guthrum accepts his invitation,

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:07.200
and I will watch for him
and I shall ride out and meet him.

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:09.320
I will pass on your message, Lord.

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:16.040
This horse belongs to me now.

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:22.800
Uhtred, Alfred is keen
to find a use for you,

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:24.760
but Brida is...

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:26.320
She's not a help.

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:28.360
Perhaps you could just
keep her away from him.

00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:30.280
Alfred knows how I can be of use.

00:20:30.360 --> 00:20:31.640
-Uhtred.
-And I have proven it.

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:33.600
Now he must prove he can be of use to me.

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:34.920
He will be king.

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:36.200
And you can serve him.

00:20:36.280 --> 00:20:38.160
I'm here to serve myself.

00:20:38.240 --> 00:20:41.320
Alfred means nothing to me but a path
to take back what's rightfully mine.

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:44.200
My land, my wealth and my title.

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:47.480
He will have a use for me,
but I will have a use for him.

00:20:47.560 --> 00:20:49.640
Do not think him naive.

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:51.000
He will see right through you.

00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:54.320
He will see what I allow him to see.

00:20:55.960 --> 00:20:59.280
Look, Uhtred, right now
you are a warrior, not a thinker.

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:02.160
Though in time, this will come.

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:05.720
You are much like your father,
and he was both.

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:08.120
You are Alfred's priest now, Beocca.

00:21:17.840 --> 00:21:20.120
[man] You looking for company, girl?

00:21:20.200 --> 00:21:23.640
I prefer the company of the gods
to stupid men.

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:26.280
Another time, then?

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:32.400
[snickers]

00:22:53.880 --> 00:22:56.480
[knocking]

00:22:58.120 --> 00:22:59.280
Good morning, Uhtred.

00:22:59.360 --> 00:23:00.680
Good morning, Lord.

00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:11.560
That's a fine coat of mail.

00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:13.400
It is. And it is yours.

00:23:13.480 --> 00:23:16.240
The battle dress of a Saxon warrior,
a gift.

00:23:16.320 --> 00:23:17.640
In return for what?

00:23:17.720 --> 00:23:19.360
There's always a price.

00:23:19.440 --> 00:23:23.080
Which you have paid in full,
our victory at the hill.

00:23:23.160 --> 00:23:27.040
Young Odda, have you offered
your apologies to Uhtred?

00:23:29.200 --> 00:23:32.520
My sincere apologies, you spoke the truth.

00:23:33.840 --> 00:23:36.320
A small bow, perhaps?

00:23:42.080 --> 00:23:43.800
You may leave us now.

00:23:49.800 --> 00:23:54.200
A good king relies upon
good advice, Uhtred.

00:23:54.280 --> 00:23:57.960
For example, my nephew,
Aethelwold, the king's son.

00:23:58.040 --> 00:24:01.040
He is young, but sees himself
as the rightful heir.

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:02.680
How am I to deal with him?

00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:07.680
You should kill him, Lord,

00:24:07.760 --> 00:24:10.640
as my own Uncle Aelfric, would kill me.

00:24:10.720 --> 00:24:12.320
Not to kill him shows weakness.

00:24:12.400 --> 00:24:13.720
[Odda] You are being insolent.

00:24:13.800 --> 00:24:17.200
I will allow it,
it is the Pagan in him speaking.

00:24:17.280 --> 00:24:19.520
You think like a Dane, Uhtred.

00:24:19.600 --> 00:24:21.400
If I kill Aethelwold,

00:24:21.480 --> 00:24:24.040
I am admitting he has legitimate claim
to the throne,

00:24:24.120 --> 00:24:25.120
which he does not.

00:24:25.200 --> 00:24:26.800
That is how I think.

00:24:28.080 --> 00:24:30.480
But to have a specimen
of the heathen mind in council

00:24:30.560 --> 00:24:31.560
will be useful.

00:24:32.800 --> 00:24:35.720
What do they fear most, the Danes?

00:24:36.720 --> 00:24:38.480
They're warriors, they live to fight.

00:24:38.560 --> 00:24:41.080
But when they lose,
as at the hill, what then?

00:24:41.160 --> 00:24:44.600
In battle, they'd rather retreat
than lose too many men.

00:24:44.680 --> 00:24:47.160
So if they fear anything at all,
it's losing men.

00:24:47.240 --> 00:24:51.720
They love to fight but hate to lose,
hardly a revelation.

00:24:51.800 --> 00:24:54.520
-Odda appears not to value your council.
-I do not!

00:24:54.600 --> 00:24:55.600
I care not.

00:24:55.680 --> 00:24:59.000
I have been thinking on your request,
to be recognized as an Aelderman.

00:24:59.080 --> 00:25:00.360
[Odda] Which is a nonsense.

00:25:00.440 --> 00:25:01.680
I am an Aelderman.

00:25:01.760 --> 00:25:03.360
Without even a goat to your name,

00:25:03.440 --> 00:25:04.960
never mind the land to graze it.

00:25:05.040 --> 00:25:06.480
I am an Aelderman by birth, Lord.

00:25:06.560 --> 00:25:09.200
Would you perhaps consider
becoming an Aelderman by marriage?

00:25:09.280 --> 00:25:12.360
I know of a marriage
that would bring you land and title.

00:25:12.440 --> 00:25:14.040
I have no need of a wife, Lord.

00:25:14.120 --> 00:25:15.720
-A woman helps you grow.
-Grow old?

00:25:15.800 --> 00:25:17.920
Grow roots,
and that is what you are missing.

00:25:18.880 --> 00:25:22.240
Marriage would show
your commitment to Wessex.

00:25:22.320 --> 00:25:24.000
I have shown commitment.

00:25:24.080 --> 00:25:27.160
You've said yourself,
I gave you victory at the hill.

00:25:27.240 --> 00:25:30.320
You helped, Uhtred, but the victory
was won by the men of Wessex.

00:25:30.400 --> 00:25:32.880
Whom you now refuse to join,
through this marriage.

00:25:32.960 --> 00:25:36.200
Land and silver is what all men desire,
and I'm no different.

00:25:36.280 --> 00:25:39.040
But believe me, Lord,
I have no need of a wife.

00:25:40.160 --> 00:25:41.360
My sword is yours.

00:25:41.440 --> 00:25:43.280
[Odda] At a price?

00:25:43.360 --> 00:25:47.080
Everything that I have
has been taken from me.

00:25:48.360 --> 00:25:50.600
I need title, I need to make my wealth.

00:25:50.680 --> 00:25:52.040
Are you offering me your sword,

00:25:52.120 --> 00:25:54.320
or are you selling me your sword?

00:25:54.400 --> 00:25:58.080
To become an Aelderman,
you must possess land.

00:25:58.160 --> 00:25:59.240
That is the law.

00:25:59.320 --> 00:26:04.200
However, stand at my side
during the negotiations ahead,

00:26:04.280 --> 00:26:06.920
help me read my enemy,

00:26:07.000 --> 00:26:12.320
and in return, we shall talk further
of wealth and reward.

00:26:27.800 --> 00:26:28.800
[gasps]

00:26:28.880 --> 00:26:30.200
[laughs]

00:26:35.240 --> 00:26:37.120
Well, what did you see?

00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:39.080
What did they show you?

00:26:39.160 --> 00:26:40.760
What I saw is my business.

00:26:40.840 --> 00:26:42.280
[groans] I feel unwell.

00:26:48.720 --> 00:26:49.880
Here...

00:26:51.840 --> 00:26:53.040
Water.

00:27:09.520 --> 00:27:12.520
Where we find ourselves is fate.

00:27:13.600 --> 00:27:15.640
The work of the three spinners.

00:27:15.720 --> 00:27:19.360
They sit deep in this earth beneath us
and they have brought us here.

00:27:20.840 --> 00:27:22.680
We should go...

00:27:24.200 --> 00:27:28.320
...to Cornwalum, Wales, Ireland.

00:27:28.400 --> 00:27:29.400
Anywhere.

00:27:29.480 --> 00:27:30.480
Why?

00:27:30.560 --> 00:27:32.280
Escape.

00:27:36.400 --> 00:27:37.960
Safety.

00:27:40.680 --> 00:27:42.560
I saw Ragnar's ship.

00:27:42.640 --> 00:27:43.720
The past?

00:27:43.800 --> 00:27:45.800
No, Wind Viper.

00:27:47.280 --> 00:27:48.680
Young Ragnar?

00:27:48.760 --> 00:27:51.360
I was there on the ship. I saw it.

00:27:52.720 --> 00:27:54.280
I want to leave here.

00:27:55.280 --> 00:27:56.600
Come with me.

00:27:59.320 --> 00:28:01.120
Come with me.

00:28:01.200 --> 00:28:03.280
I've given a promise to Alfred...

00:28:04.800 --> 00:28:07.160
...to attend the negotiations, to advise.

00:28:13.040 --> 00:28:16.080
Brida, there's no place else for us to go.

00:28:16.160 --> 00:28:18.240
We cannot stay here!

00:28:20.400 --> 00:28:21.760
It's a beginning.

00:28:25.840 --> 00:28:27.280
Leave me.

00:28:28.800 --> 00:28:32.040
We can not wander the country
and do nothing.

00:28:32.120 --> 00:28:33.840
How can you trust him?

00:28:33.920 --> 00:28:36.520
How do you know he won't
simply turn you over to Guthrum,

00:28:36.600 --> 00:28:37.600
to pass on to Ubba?

00:28:37.680 --> 00:28:38.880
You know nothing about him!

00:28:38.960 --> 00:28:41.600
I trust Father Beocca,
and Beocca is his priest.

00:28:41.680 --> 00:28:43.440
I said leave me!

00:28:49.960 --> 00:28:52.120
You were not on the ship with me!

00:28:53.280 --> 00:28:55.760
Go to Alfred,
and I will watch him betray you!

00:29:15.400 --> 00:29:18.440
So what do we know of this Alfred?

00:29:18.520 --> 00:29:20.880
That he is sickly, he's weak.

00:29:20.960 --> 00:29:22.680
He wants to negotiate.

00:29:23.720 --> 00:29:25.920
Turns out that he's no warrior.

00:29:27.400 --> 00:29:28.880
But he beat you, Guthrum.

00:29:28.960 --> 00:29:30.400
[chuckles]

00:29:34.720 --> 00:29:37.640
So, what does it say?

00:29:50.760 --> 00:29:52.320
Negotiation.

00:29:54.240 --> 00:29:55.920
Silver.

00:29:56.000 --> 00:29:58.240
We will take his silver...

00:30:00.240 --> 00:30:01.920
...and his land.

00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:03.560
And if he refuses?

00:30:03.640 --> 00:30:05.000
He will never refuse.

00:30:05.080 --> 00:30:08.560
He wants to live
and he wants to be called king.

00:30:08.640 --> 00:30:09.640
[chuckles]

00:31:27.640 --> 00:31:28.960
[crowd murmuring]

00:31:36.720 --> 00:31:38.640
Our God, in His Heaven,

00:31:38.720 --> 00:31:41.000
we ask you to find favor

00:31:41.080 --> 00:31:44.280
with your devoted servant, Alfred.

00:31:45.240 --> 00:31:48.640
Bless him with courage,
strength and wisdom.

00:31:48.720 --> 00:31:51.520
Never leave his side. Amen.

00:31:51.600 --> 00:31:52.880
[all] Amen.

00:31:52.960 --> 00:31:57.120
Allow him pure and holy thoughts

00:31:57.200 --> 00:32:01.800
and the power to carry out your work
on this earth as our king.

00:32:03.200 --> 00:32:07.520
Allow this anointing of Alfred
to enable your will.

00:32:08.440 --> 00:32:12.120
You are God's king, Alfred of Wessex.

00:32:12.200 --> 00:32:15.280
<i>Vivat Rex Alfredus!</i>

00:32:15.360 --> 00:32:18.480
[all]<i> Vivat Rex Alfredus!</i>

00:32:18.560 --> 00:32:21.720
<i>Vivat Rex Alfredus!</i>

00:32:21.800 --> 00:32:25.360
<i>Vivat Rex Alfredus!</i>

00:32:25.440 --> 00:32:28.040
[chanting continues]

00:32:37.920 --> 00:32:41.040
[chanting continues]

00:32:47.560 --> 00:32:50.560
[all continue chanting]
<i>Vivat Rex Alfredus!</i>

00:32:52.960 --> 00:32:55.480
I can't imagine a time without you.

00:33:10.920 --> 00:33:12.240
[moaning]

00:33:25.960 --> 00:33:28.040
It is Guthrum?

00:33:28.120 --> 00:33:29.400
Yes.

00:33:29.480 --> 00:33:32.040
You can see a bone in his hair.

00:33:32.920 --> 00:33:34.560
It's his mother's rib.

00:33:35.880 --> 00:33:37.560
How endearing.

00:33:37.640 --> 00:33:38.880
And the others?

00:33:38.960 --> 00:33:42.320
It's Ubba. The big man.

00:33:42.400 --> 00:33:44.320
The chieftain Ubba is with them?

00:33:44.400 --> 00:33:45.760
You said he was in the north.

00:33:46.680 --> 00:33:47.960
And now he is here.

00:33:50.240 --> 00:33:51.640
This is good.

00:34:12.080 --> 00:34:14.840
[Guthrum] So you are Alfred,
the King of Wessex?

00:34:14.920 --> 00:34:17.840
I am. You are Earl Guthrum?

00:34:17.920 --> 00:34:21.680
Yes. If you want peace,
you'll have to pay.

00:34:23.120 --> 00:34:24.600
And you are the Earl Ubba?

00:34:24.680 --> 00:34:26.000
Welcome.

00:34:26.080 --> 00:34:27.320
Speak.

00:34:27.400 --> 00:34:30.040
[Alfred] In exchange for an agreed amount

00:34:30.120 --> 00:34:31.520
of grain, livestock and silver,

00:34:31.600 --> 00:34:34.760
I propose that you and your ships return
to Lundene and remain there.

00:34:34.840 --> 00:34:37.360
I further propose that
you confine yourselves

00:34:37.440 --> 00:34:39.880
to East Anglia, Mercia and Northumbria.

00:34:39.960 --> 00:34:44.320
Wessex is Saxon, and as such,
out-of-bounds to all Danes.

00:34:44.400 --> 00:34:46.440
We'll not be leaving Wessex.

00:34:46.520 --> 00:34:48.240
We only just arrived.

00:34:48.320 --> 00:34:49.480
Then you will starve.

00:34:51.160 --> 00:34:52.760
You have little food...

00:34:52.840 --> 00:34:55.720
no shelter and a weakened army.

00:34:55.800 --> 00:34:58.560
If you believe us weakened,
why seek peace?

00:34:59.480 --> 00:35:03.440
It's the Christian in me,
the will of my God.

00:35:03.520 --> 00:35:05.000
Oh, I will hear no talk of gods.

00:35:05.080 --> 00:35:07.160
God. There is only one.

00:35:07.240 --> 00:35:12.400
You will talk of grain, horses,
silver and land.

00:35:12.480 --> 00:35:13.480
I will not talk of land.

00:35:13.560 --> 00:35:16.200
What do they write?

00:35:16.280 --> 00:35:17.840
[Alfred] They write what we speak.

00:35:17.920 --> 00:35:18.960
Every word?

00:35:19.040 --> 00:35:20.560
Yes, every word.

00:35:20.640 --> 00:35:23.000
Then may I say arse...

00:35:23.080 --> 00:35:24.880
tits, hump and turd?

00:35:24.960 --> 00:35:28.000
They record history.
We are here creating history.

00:35:28.080 --> 00:35:30.640
People will read of this very meeting.

00:35:30.720 --> 00:35:33.000
I'm waiting to hear
the terms of your surrender.

00:35:33.080 --> 00:35:35.160
You will be paid
for your return to Lundene.

00:35:35.240 --> 00:35:38.840
There are no more terms
and there will be no surrender.

00:35:38.920 --> 00:35:43.560
Guthrum, here, will not leave Readingum.

00:35:43.640 --> 00:35:45.640
Then I say again, he will starve.

00:35:45.720 --> 00:35:48.600
We will raid, we will kill.

00:35:48.680 --> 00:35:50.480
And you will lose yet more men.

00:35:50.560 --> 00:35:55.360
Is that your wish, Earl Guthrum?
To lose men.

00:35:55.440 --> 00:35:59.760
Your surviving warriors
may look to find a new Lord.

00:35:59.840 --> 00:36:01.600
Did you call a meeting to insult me?

00:36:01.680 --> 00:36:04.000
I offer peace, and I offer facts.

00:36:06.200 --> 00:36:08.560
[Ubba] His head and you can have
your peace.

00:36:09.680 --> 00:36:10.840
Him.

00:36:17.960 --> 00:36:21.400
Uhtred Ragnarson.

00:36:21.480 --> 00:36:23.320
A traitor.

00:36:29.640 --> 00:36:31.800
Nothing to say?

00:36:31.880 --> 00:36:33.640
I'll speak to Young Ragnar.

00:36:34.640 --> 00:36:37.280
No other Dane has my respect.

00:36:37.360 --> 00:36:39.480
His head... for peace.

00:36:39.560 --> 00:36:41.280
You want Uhtred here for peace.

00:36:41.360 --> 00:36:44.960
No silver, no grain, no horses?

00:36:45.040 --> 00:36:48.720
We want silver... and the traitor's head.

00:36:48.800 --> 00:36:51.880
These are the terms, and you, Alfred...

00:36:51.960 --> 00:36:53.840
you may remain king.

00:36:53.920 --> 00:36:58.480
But we will occupy all of the Saxon forts.

00:36:58.560 --> 00:37:02.880
If you wish to occupy the fortresses,
then do it, take them.

00:37:04.040 --> 00:37:06.480
How many have you taken to date?

00:37:07.600 --> 00:37:09.360
Father, how many have they taken to date?

00:37:10.000 --> 00:37:11.400
None, Lord.

00:37:14.400 --> 00:37:16.720
We can take all the fortresses
at any time!

00:37:16.800 --> 00:37:19.840
We have taken the whole of England!

00:37:21.760 --> 00:37:25.480
And we can do the same with Wessex.

00:37:25.560 --> 00:37:26.560
Let me be clear.

00:37:26.640 --> 00:37:30.640
I am prepared to return to the sword,
we outnumber you.

00:37:30.720 --> 00:37:32.080
We are many and we are dangerous.

00:37:32.160 --> 00:37:34.880
But I would prefer to establish a peace.

00:37:34.960 --> 00:37:37.200
And Uhtred here shall keep his head,

00:37:37.280 --> 00:37:40.680
but I will pay you well to leave Wessex.

00:37:41.680 --> 00:37:45.160
That is what people will read,
that Alfred sought peace.

00:37:46.440 --> 00:37:51.480
Alfred paid Lords Ubba and Guthrum
in silver in exchange for peace.

00:37:51.560 --> 00:37:55.280
It is I, who is seeking an end
to the fighting.

00:37:55.360 --> 00:37:58.040
That is what will be written.

00:38:20.280 --> 00:38:21.400
Uhtred.

00:38:26.320 --> 00:38:30.000
I would never have given you up...
to Ubba.

00:38:30.080 --> 00:38:32.440
But the thought did cross your mind, Lord.

00:38:32.520 --> 00:38:34.160
Not once.

00:38:34.240 --> 00:38:38.480
The fact is, I would like you
to swear an oath,

00:38:38.560 --> 00:38:41.880
on holy relics, a year's service.

00:38:42.880 --> 00:38:45.560
During which time you will help
my warriors understand

00:38:45.640 --> 00:38:49.160
that the heathens are but men.

00:38:49.240 --> 00:38:51.640
And in return, and in time,

00:38:51.720 --> 00:38:53.840
you shall have your own reward,

00:38:53.920 --> 00:38:56.320
Uhtred of Bebbanburg.

00:38:59.600 --> 00:39:01.040
One year.

00:39:38.560 --> 00:39:39.960
[man] Boy.

00:39:48.800 --> 00:39:50.440
For the king.

00:40:02.040 --> 00:40:04.760
[Alfred] They have been halted
but nothing more.

00:40:05.800 --> 00:40:07.760
[Alfred] They are not defeated.

00:40:08.880 --> 00:40:11.560
Our task now is both simple
and impossible.

00:40:11.640 --> 00:40:13.480
We determine what they will do next.

00:40:13.560 --> 00:40:15.400
They will do what Danes always do, attack.

00:40:15.480 --> 00:40:16.800
How? Where? When? How many?

00:40:16.880 --> 00:40:19.000
We are supposed to be celebrating a peace.

00:40:19.080 --> 00:40:20.640
Do we have to talk of fighting?

00:40:20.720 --> 00:40:23.640
[Alfred] We do, my dear,
because the peace will not last.

00:40:24.600 --> 00:40:26.160
It'll take them at least a year

00:40:26.240 --> 00:40:28.560
before they can gather
a second great army.

00:40:28.640 --> 00:40:30.120
-Do we have your word?
-[Odda] Son.

00:40:30.200 --> 00:40:31.680
Is there any meat here?

00:40:31.760 --> 00:40:33.600
Should she even be here?

00:40:33.680 --> 00:40:34.800
Brida is my guest.

00:40:34.880 --> 00:40:39.040
You should have taken up
the king's offer of a wife, a lady.

00:40:39.120 --> 00:40:42.800
[Alfred] What happens next, I believe,
is that they will come by land and sea.

00:40:42.880 --> 00:40:45.320
They will split our army in two,
possibly more.

00:40:45.400 --> 00:40:49.560
Now Uhtred may be correct,
this may not occur for a year or more,

00:40:49.640 --> 00:40:52.640
but what is clear is that we need ships.

00:40:53.840 --> 00:40:57.040
We are bordered by water
yet we have so few ships.

00:40:57.120 --> 00:40:58.920
You'll not get me on a ship.

00:40:59.000 --> 00:41:00.880
I'll volunteer my son.

00:41:00.960 --> 00:41:03.880
To save our shores,
we have to look beyond them.

00:41:03.960 --> 00:41:08.200
And to serve God... his word must travel.

00:41:08.280 --> 00:41:10.040
Amen. Praise him.

00:41:10.120 --> 00:41:13.880
Uhtred, the beasts
on the prows of Danes ships,

00:41:13.960 --> 00:41:17.440
they are a representation of their gods?

00:41:17.520 --> 00:41:19.160
No, Lord. They are just beasts.

00:41:19.240 --> 00:41:21.040
They can be lifted from their posts,

00:41:21.120 --> 00:41:23.080
so not to frighten
the spirits of the land.

00:41:23.160 --> 00:41:25.080
Spirits of the land.

00:41:25.160 --> 00:41:28.840
I would like to know why some of them
make their own teeth into points.

00:41:28.920 --> 00:41:30.000
They do that?

00:41:30.080 --> 00:41:31.400
Some, lady.

00:41:31.480 --> 00:41:32.720
God save us.

00:41:32.800 --> 00:41:35.120
To show that they aren't afraid.

00:41:35.200 --> 00:41:37.760
If they can inflict
such pain on themselves,

00:41:37.840 --> 00:41:39.320
think what they might do to a Saxon.

00:41:39.400 --> 00:41:42.200
[Alfred] We will understand them
more by the day, I'm sure.

00:41:42.280 --> 00:41:46.720
Uhtred-of-the-Danes has promised me
a year of his service.

00:41:47.720 --> 00:41:49.160
Is that so?

00:41:49.240 --> 00:41:50.440
It is.

00:41:50.520 --> 00:41:53.480
It will be his responsibility
to show our warriors

00:41:53.560 --> 00:41:55.960
how the Danes approach battle,

00:41:56.040 --> 00:41:58.880
the construction of their shield wall
and the like.

00:41:58.960 --> 00:42:00.760
Lord, if I may.

00:42:00.840 --> 00:42:02.600
The arseling here is barely a man.

00:42:03.720 --> 00:42:05.800
You expect him to teach me how to fight?

00:42:05.880 --> 00:42:08.720
Leofric, I expect him
to teach you nothing.

00:42:09.560 --> 00:42:13.360
Whip him with staves in practice,
by all means.

00:42:13.440 --> 00:42:14.880
Thank you, Lord.

00:42:14.960 --> 00:42:17.680
But our lesser men,

00:42:17.760 --> 00:42:20.560
if they can know what a Dane knows...

00:42:21.560 --> 00:42:24.600
...fear can be expelled with knowledge.

00:42:25.520 --> 00:42:27.960
Regardless how sharp their teeth.

00:42:41.320 --> 00:42:43.320
You didn't eat tonight.

00:42:43.400 --> 00:42:45.120
I'd only throw it up.

00:42:46.400 --> 00:42:47.800
A year?

00:42:47.880 --> 00:42:49.680
[sighs]

00:42:49.760 --> 00:42:52.400
It starts with a year
and becomes a lifetime.

00:42:54.240 --> 00:42:55.840
And he offered you a wife?

00:42:55.920 --> 00:42:57.640
I have no need of a wife.

00:42:57.720 --> 00:42:59.480
Instead you swore an oath to kill Danes.

00:42:59.560 --> 00:43:01.880
You know my reasons.

00:43:03.280 --> 00:43:04.960
We have been living in a palace.

00:43:06.520 --> 00:43:11.040
What happens if you find yourself
facing Young Ragnar... in battle?

00:43:15.520 --> 00:43:16.880
We fight.

00:43:28.480 --> 00:43:30.040
[indistinct chatter]

00:43:44.680 --> 00:43:47.880
Where is she?
I haven't heard her at all morning.

00:43:47.960 --> 00:43:49.320
She'll not be far.

00:43:50.320 --> 00:43:51.800
Well, were about to leave.

00:43:51.880 --> 00:43:53.320
I can see.

00:43:54.520 --> 00:43:55.960
I'll follow.

00:44:03.800 --> 00:44:05.920
[groaning]

00:44:31.280 --> 00:44:32.800
[Uhtred] Brida!

00:44:42.080 --> 00:44:43.880
Brida!

00:44:56.160 --> 00:44:58.560
Brida!

00:45:05.600 --> 00:45:06.840
Brida?

00:45:17.520 --> 00:45:19.720
Almost a child.

00:45:23.280 --> 00:45:24.800
You knew?

00:45:24.880 --> 00:45:26.280
Hmm?

00:45:26.360 --> 00:45:27.800
That you were carrying?

00:45:34.000 --> 00:45:35.400
No.

00:45:36.320 --> 00:45:40.640
You didn't see it in your dreams,
when you drank the mushroom ale?

00:45:44.680 --> 00:45:46.440
[sighs]

00:45:47.400 --> 00:45:48.800
I'll bury it.

00:45:51.320 --> 00:45:54.280
We'll bury it, it's a sign of a passing.

00:46:03.680 --> 00:46:04.680
Stand together!

00:46:04.760 --> 00:46:06.120
[Uhtred] Shields front!

00:46:06.200 --> 00:46:07.360
Shields up!

00:46:07.440 --> 00:46:08.600
Shields together!

00:46:08.680 --> 00:46:11.200
-Look them in the eye!
-Closer together! Unbreakable!

00:46:11.280 --> 00:46:13.560
-[Leofric] Are we ready?!
-[all cheering]

00:46:13.640 --> 00:46:15.680
I say, are we ready?

00:46:15.760 --> 00:46:17.440
[man] Forward!
-[all shouting]

00:46:19.400 --> 00:46:21.560
Kill the bastards!

00:46:21.640 --> 00:46:22.920
Stand together!

00:46:23.000 --> 00:46:24.680
[all shouting]

00:46:26.920 --> 00:46:28.240
[grunting]

00:46:29.120 --> 00:46:31.840
[Uhtred] Shields together!

00:46:31.920 --> 00:46:33.560
We hammer them with our shields!

00:46:33.640 --> 00:46:35.400
They are our defense and our weapon!

00:46:35.480 --> 00:46:37.240
We knock them off their feet!

00:46:37.320 --> 00:46:38.840
We're a wall!

00:46:38.920 --> 00:46:40.960
[all grunting in unison]

00:46:45.280 --> 00:46:46.920
Charge!

00:46:58.000 --> 00:47:00.440
Before the two walls meet,

00:47:00.520 --> 00:47:02.600
the first three rows of men act together

00:47:02.680 --> 00:47:04.320
to create a tall shield wall.

00:47:04.400 --> 00:47:06.280
First row crouches lower,

00:47:06.360 --> 00:47:08.320
protecting the lower body and legs.

00:47:08.400 --> 00:47:12.400
The second row reaches forward,
protecting the upper body.

00:47:12.480 --> 00:47:17.520
The third row leans in protecting
the head of all rows of men.

00:47:17.600 --> 00:47:19.120
Shields up!

00:47:20.800 --> 00:47:22.360
Shields together!

00:47:23.520 --> 00:47:25.440
Shield wall!

00:47:29.960 --> 00:47:33.360
I like it, arseling. I do.

00:47:34.800 --> 00:47:36.600
Now kill the bastard!

00:47:36.680 --> 00:47:38.360
[all shouting]

00:47:40.760 --> 00:47:41.560
[digging]

00:47:53.320 --> 00:47:55.240
[horse approaching]

00:47:57.720 --> 00:47:59.120
The wealth isn't mine.

00:48:00.520 --> 00:48:02.680
It belongs to Lord Ragnar the Fearless.

00:48:02.760 --> 00:48:06.120
You will do well to leave me alone.

00:48:06.200 --> 00:48:08.120
[man] Are you Brida?

00:48:09.000 --> 00:48:10.120
Who asks?

00:48:11.440 --> 00:48:12.720
[indistinct chatter]

00:48:14.640 --> 00:48:16.280
Brida.

00:48:16.360 --> 00:48:17.600
What of her?

00:48:19.360 --> 00:48:23.360
I'm no seer, but I'd say she's unhappy.

00:48:24.880 --> 00:48:27.400
She prefers the company of Danes
to Saxons.

00:48:28.720 --> 00:48:29.720
Nothing wrong in that.

00:48:30.800 --> 00:48:32.480
She's been with the wrong Saxons.

00:48:32.560 --> 00:48:34.640
The Danes have a hunger for life.

00:48:34.720 --> 00:48:36.240
Don't we all?

00:48:37.280 --> 00:48:41.720
Alfred... he's serious.

00:48:41.800 --> 00:48:43.200
[scoffs]

00:48:43.280 --> 00:48:45.320
A pious bastard.

00:48:45.400 --> 00:48:49.680
Dislike him, by all means,
but never underestimate him.

00:48:50.800 --> 00:48:52.080
He is ruthless.

00:48:52.160 --> 00:48:55.120
And the man thinks...

00:48:55.200 --> 00:48:57.480
which is more than you or I could do.

00:48:57.560 --> 00:49:01.440
Leofric the Warrior, may I sit with you?

00:49:01.520 --> 00:49:03.360
No, you may not.

00:49:03.440 --> 00:49:05.120
Do the monks know you're missing?

00:49:06.720 --> 00:49:10.680
Uhtred, this is Aethelwold,
another arseling.

00:49:11.680 --> 00:49:12.560
Nephew of the king.

00:49:12.640 --> 00:49:15.280
No, I am not the nephew of the king.

00:49:15.360 --> 00:49:17.920
I am the king.

00:49:19.560 --> 00:49:20.880
But Alfred likes to pretend,

00:49:20.960 --> 00:49:23.240
and every bastard
appears to be happy with the lie.

00:49:23.320 --> 00:49:24.720
[chuckles]

00:49:26.160 --> 00:49:27.440
What are we talking about?

00:49:27.520 --> 00:49:28.520
Alfred.

00:49:28.600 --> 00:49:31.120
He will not allow me to fight!
Have I told you that?

00:49:31.200 --> 00:49:32.440
Many times.

00:49:32.520 --> 00:49:35.160
Well, it's true.
He will not allow me to fight.

00:49:35.240 --> 00:49:38.360
I would like you, Warrior Leofric,

00:49:38.440 --> 00:49:42.720
to teach me how to fight,
and I shall teach you how to...

00:49:42.800 --> 00:49:44.200
Go on.

00:49:44.280 --> 00:49:46.080
You will not forget to pay for this.

00:49:46.160 --> 00:49:48.400
Have I ever?

00:49:48.480 --> 00:49:50.000
Once or twice.

00:50:00.640 --> 00:50:02.920
Alfred was caught humping a nun once.

00:50:03.000 --> 00:50:04.960
[choking]

00:50:05.040 --> 00:50:07.880
What I ought to do is slit his gizzard.

00:50:09.120 --> 00:50:11.680
Say that to anyone but me, boy,
and you'll be hanged.

00:50:11.760 --> 00:50:13.600
You are hurting royalty.

00:50:17.320 --> 00:50:20.040
You are lucky
Alfred hasn't had you killed.

00:50:20.120 --> 00:50:21.920
God will not allow him.

00:50:23.320 --> 00:50:24.520
I like God.

00:50:29.960 --> 00:50:32.440
[Uhtred makes clucking sound]

00:50:53.360 --> 00:50:55.240
The silver?

00:50:55.320 --> 00:50:57.480
Yes.

00:50:57.560 --> 00:50:59.440
Why?

00:51:01.360 --> 00:51:02.520
Are you leaving me?

00:51:02.600 --> 00:51:03.920
Are you drunk?

00:51:05.600 --> 00:51:07.400
Maybe a little.

00:51:07.480 --> 00:51:09.720
We will give the silver to Young Ragnar.

00:51:11.600 --> 00:51:14.320
Tomorrow, dusk.

00:51:16.880 --> 00:51:18.720
He's here.

00:51:20.080 --> 00:51:22.600
We can tell him the truth...

00:51:22.680 --> 00:51:25.160
and we can join Ragnar and his men.

00:51:32.600 --> 00:51:34.680
I need men bound to me by God,

00:51:34.760 --> 00:51:37.960
by duty, by the land, by Wessex itself.

00:51:38.040 --> 00:51:42.200
I would again like to put to Uhtred
the prospect of marriage.

00:51:42.280 --> 00:51:43.840
To my goddaughter?

00:51:43.920 --> 00:51:45.160
To Mildrith, yes.

00:51:46.280 --> 00:51:48.360
Well, it would certainly bind him
to the land

00:51:48.440 --> 00:51:50.760
and indirectly, to the church, to God.

00:51:50.840 --> 00:51:51.840
It would test him.

00:51:51.920 --> 00:51:53.680
It would.

00:51:53.760 --> 00:51:56.120
You would be in favor, still?

00:51:56.200 --> 00:51:59.600
Of course, anything for Wessex.

00:52:07.320 --> 00:52:08.440
[birds chirping]

00:52:13.600 --> 00:52:16.800
Uhtred Ragnarson is a good man to be.

00:52:18.440 --> 00:52:19.960
Look at me.

00:52:20.040 --> 00:52:22.040
You owe Alfred nothing.

00:52:22.120 --> 00:52:24.480
To him your word means nothing,
you're a Pagan.

00:52:25.480 --> 00:52:26.800
Please.

00:52:35.880 --> 00:52:40.680
Uhtred Ragnarson can never become
Uhtred of Bebbanburg.

00:52:43.800 --> 00:52:45.360
Never.

00:52:47.520 --> 00:52:49.320
[rustling]

00:52:55.720 --> 00:52:57.840
Did you kill my father?

00:52:59.000 --> 00:53:00.200
Do you need to ask?

00:53:00.280 --> 00:53:03.440
Did you kill my family?

00:53:03.520 --> 00:53:04.680
He didn't.

00:53:04.760 --> 00:53:06.880
I'm speaking with Uhtred!

00:53:09.760 --> 00:53:12.840
I won't ask a second time.

00:53:17.960 --> 00:53:20.760
If you believe that
I would kill our father,

00:53:20.840 --> 00:53:24.520
our mother and our family...

00:53:28.200 --> 00:53:30.000
...take your revenge.

00:53:38.400 --> 00:53:42.560
I knew it. I knew it.

00:53:43.840 --> 00:53:45.360
I had to be sure, I knew it.

00:53:46.560 --> 00:53:48.680
[breathes deeply]

00:53:52.480 --> 00:53:54.600
It was Kjartan.

00:53:54.680 --> 00:53:57.200
Kjartan attacked and set the fire.

00:53:57.280 --> 00:53:59.080
If we could have saved them,
we would have.

00:53:59.160 --> 00:54:00.200
I knew it.

00:54:00.280 --> 00:54:02.320
I didn't believe a word I was hearing.

00:54:02.400 --> 00:54:06.440
We have Ragnar's wealth,
we kept it for you.

00:54:08.120 --> 00:54:10.120
[chuckles] Brida.

00:54:10.200 --> 00:54:12.560
Fully grown woman now!

00:54:18.640 --> 00:54:22.440
I've seen this moment in my dreams
so many times.

00:54:24.960 --> 00:54:27.520
[Young Ragnar] So, Kjartan's story
is that the English

00:54:27.600 --> 00:54:31.200
rose against our father,
encouraged by you.

00:54:32.840 --> 00:54:35.920
He claims to have revenged himself
for the killers.

00:54:36.000 --> 00:54:37.400
[soft chuckle]

00:54:37.480 --> 00:54:39.280
Did you ever believe him?

00:54:40.240 --> 00:54:41.680
[chuckles]

00:54:41.760 --> 00:54:43.120
Never.

00:54:44.240 --> 00:54:46.000
But he is Lord Kjartan now.

00:54:46.080 --> 00:54:49.640
He has three times the men
and the ear of Ubba.

00:54:54.720 --> 00:54:57.520
When I kill him,
it will need to be planned.

00:54:58.680 --> 00:55:00.160
When we kill him.

00:55:01.120 --> 00:55:03.120
It will be dangerous.

00:55:03.200 --> 00:55:04.320
It must be done.

00:55:04.400 --> 00:55:06.400
Ragnar, we're with you.

00:55:08.720 --> 00:55:10.880
Then you will sail with me?

00:55:13.240 --> 00:55:14.640
I will.

00:55:16.840 --> 00:55:18.560
I have sworn to Alfred.

00:55:19.600 --> 00:55:21.040
It means nothing.

00:55:24.280 --> 00:55:26.120
Well, if you have sworn...

00:55:28.960 --> 00:55:30.320
...then you must keep your word.

00:55:41.880 --> 00:55:44.560
I need this revenge like I need water.

00:55:45.840 --> 00:55:49.280
When the time is right,
I swear I'll be with you.

00:55:50.160 --> 00:55:52.000
I know.

00:56:00.080 --> 00:56:03.240
I can't believe I'm about to let you go...

00:56:04.320 --> 00:56:05.800
...lose you.

00:56:09.040 --> 00:56:11.520
You have been half my life...

00:56:14.440 --> 00:56:16.480
...all of my madness.

00:56:27.120 --> 00:56:28.800
Be happy.

00:56:57.000 --> 00:56:59.160
[Leofric] I take it she has gone, then?

00:57:02.400 --> 00:57:05.320
I'm guessing that it's Alfred
that kept you here.

00:57:06.480 --> 00:57:08.400
I sold myself...

00:57:09.800 --> 00:57:12.120
...for a mail coat and helmet.

00:57:13.080 --> 00:57:15.680
That's what we do, we sell ourselves.

00:57:20.280 --> 00:57:25.480
This year, what you've giving to Alfred,
it's not about a mail coat.

00:57:26.480 --> 00:57:28.480
It's about you.

00:57:28.560 --> 00:57:30.720
The bastard thinks, didn't I say?

00:57:35.160 --> 00:57:38.240
He wants more than a year's service.

00:57:38.320 --> 00:57:41.560
He wants you to help take back England.

00:57:41.640 --> 00:57:43.360
All of England.

00:57:45.440 --> 00:57:48.960
Of course, when the year's up,
you could go back to the Danes.

00:57:49.960 --> 00:57:52.680
That would at least give me
the chance to kill you.

00:57:55.400 --> 00:57:57.120
But what would you be?

00:57:58.840 --> 00:58:00.840
Who would you be?